<p rendition="#et"><hi rendition="#larger">6 Ueberfluss bringt Ueberdruss.</hi> &#x2013; <hi rendition="#i">Bücking, 179; Blum, 565; Mayer, I, 168; Müller, 43, 4; Körte, 6109; Simrock, 10592; Braun, I, 4639; Masson, 243.</hi></p>                <lb/>
<p rendition="#et2"><hi rendition="#i">Engl.</hi>: Plenty makes dainty. (<hi rendition="#i">Gaal, 763.</hi>)</p>                <lb/>
<p rendition="#et2"><hi rendition="#i">Frz.</hi>: L'abondance engendre la satiété. (<hi rendition="#i">Gaal, 398.</hi>) &#x2013; Superflu, chose si necessaire. (<hi rendition="#i">Venedey, 116.</hi>)</p>                <lb/>
<p rendition="#et2"><hi rendition="#i">Holl.</hi>: De overvloed baart walging. (<hi rendition="#i">Harrebomée, II, 158<hi rendition="#sup">b</hi>.</hi>)</p>                <lb/>
<p rendition="#et2"><hi rendition="#i">It.</hi>: Del poco si gode, del toppo si affanna. &#x2013; L'abbondanza genera fastidia. (<hi rendition="#i">Pazzaglia, 25.</hi>)</p>                <lb/>
<p rendition="#et2"><hi rendition="#i">Lat.</hi>: Copia ignaviam affert. (<hi rendition="#i">Egeria, 36; Philippi, I, 93.</hi>) &#x2013; Sacietas ferociam parit. (<hi rendition="#i">Tappius, 100.</hi>) &#x2013; Sordent, quae possunt semper haberî. (<hi rendition="#i">Masson, 296.</hi>)</p>                <lb/>
